====================================================================================================
G183 -- THE n-FAMILY SEARCH: is there ANY mu-family with n(a0) that
        reconciles the deep end (g_N < 0.2 a0) and the full RAR curves?
====================================================================================================

--- PART 0: THE FAMILY AND THE WEDGE ---
  THE FAMILY (G183's own):  g_obs = g_N [1 + (g_N/a0)^(-n/2)]^(1/2)
    n = 2.000 @ a0_DE  ->  g_obs^2 = g_N^2 + a0 g_N  (the committed quadratic RAR, G071)
    deep (x->0)        ->  g_obs -> a0^(n/4) g_N^(1-n/4): deep slope 1-n/4;
    amplitude channel a0_eff = g_obs^2/g_N = a0^(n/2) g_N^(1-n/2)  (= seesaw scale at n = 2)
  THE WEDGE (G158-registered):
    deep end amplitude: a0_eff = 1.2-1.9e-10 -> n_seesaw = s/a0_eff = 0.99-1.56
    deep end slope: per-galaxy beta 0.601+-0.031 -> n = 2*beta = 1.20+-0.06 (n = 2.000 excluded at 12.7 sigma)
    full curves: n = 2.000 @ a0 = 9.3619e-11 (G071 registered pool rms 0.1454 dex, zero fitted params)
    seesaw n(a0) at the deep end's own fit a0 = 1.843e-10: n = 1.016 (n = 2.000 excluded at >= 5 sigma, joint)
    reconciliation candidates: (a) n-free family / (b) a0(z) G011 form / (c) environmental-EFE
    family deep-window slope (log g_obs vs log g_N over g_N in [1e-4, 0.2] a0_DE): (n=2.000,a0_DE) 0.507  (n=1.66,a0_ALT) 0.594  (n=1.20,a0_DE) 0.717   [data per-galaxy beta 0.601+-0.031 -> slope-consistent n ~ 1.6-1.8]
  [PASS] C0 [family] the n = 2.000 member is the committed quadratic RAR to 1e-10   g_pred(2.0, a0_DE) vs sqrt(g_N^2 + a0_DE g_N)

