--- PART 5: VERDICTS AND CONSEQUENCES ---
  V1 THE RECONCILED FIT: n* = 2.070 +- 0.208, a0* = 1.341e-10 +- 1.16e-10, pooled rms 0.1667 dex (N = 611); seesaw product n*a0 = 2.775e-10 (1.48x s_Lambda: the seesaw n(a0) = s/a0 does NOT hold at the fit)
      residuals: SPARC 0.1573 | MIGHTEE 0.1338 | HI 0.3424 | deep 0.1654 | rest 0.1698
      deep-end residual mean +0.0073 dex -- BUT the pooled mean masks the structure: MIGHTEE-deep mean -0.0465 (vs -0.151 anchored: 69% of the offset survives), SPARC-deep +0.0181, HI-deep +0.0139
      the reconciled family's deep-window slope (0.487) vs the data's measured per-galaxy beta 0.601 +- 0.031: +3.7 sigma -- the reconciled family also fails the deep-slope channel
      consistency: deep-end-alone (n 2.212, a0 1.045e-10) and full-curve-alone (SPARC: n 2.025, a0 1.385e-10; convention n = 2.000, a0_DE)
      THE SUBLUMINALITY STANDING: n* = 2.070 +- 0.208 vs the H046 n <= 2.01 kill line: +0.3 sigma ABOVE -- the reconciling family exits the framework's allowed Padé family
  [FAIL] C4 [M1 shape] the reconciled n* exceeds the framework's n = 2.01 subluminality kill line at > 2 sigma AND differs from the n = 2.000 convention at > 2 sigma (the family that reconciles the wedge does not exist inside the framework's family)   n* 2.070 +- 0.208; vs 2.01 +0.3s, vs 2.000 +0.3s
  [FAIL] C4b [M1 deep slope] the reconciled family's deep-window slope is excluded by the measured per-galaxy beta 0.601 +- 0.031 at > 5 sigma (the deep SLOPE channel stays open under the reconciled fit)   family window slope 0.487 vs 0.601 +- 0.031 (+3.7 sigma)
  V2 THE MODEL COMPARISON: winner = M2a G011 a0(z), gamma = 1 (BIC -2182.9); d_BIC vs M0 +143.8, vs M2a -6.1, vs M3 -5.4; rms M1 0.1667 / M2a 0.1667 / M3 0.1659 dex
  THE CONSEQUENCE: neither reading is decisive at BIC > 10; the honest split holds.

  V1 THE RECONCILED FIT (n-free, pooled 747 points): n* = 2.070 +- 0.208, a0* = 1.341e-10 +- 1.16e-10, rms 0.1667 dex, BIC -2176.8.  The pair does NOT sit between the two ends (deep-end-alone n 2.212 / a0 1.045e-10, full-curve-alone SPARC n 2.025 / a0 1.385e-10): it exits the framework's n <= 2 subluminal family at +0.3 sigma and its deep-window slope 0.487 is +3.7 sigma from the measured 0.601+-0.031.  Residuals: SPARC 0.1573, MIGHTEE 0.1338, HI 0.3424; the MIGHTEE-deep mean stays -0.0465 dex (69% of the -0.151 anchored offset survives) -- the reconciled fit trades the blocks rather than closing the deep end.

  V3 THE HONEST STATEMENT -- the wedge does NOT close under any candidate.  M1 (n-free): n* = 2.070 +- 0.208, a0* = 1.341e-10, rms 0.1667, BIC -2176.8 -- best of the three on the deciding statistic but OUTSIDE the framework family (+0.3 sigma above the n = 2.01 bound) and leaving MIGHTEE-deep -0.046 dex and the deep slope (+3.7 sigma) open.  M2a (G011 canonical gamma = 1): raises a0 by only 2.16% over the MIGHTEE z-gap vs the ~55-90% demanded (required gamma 12-32 vs 1; fitted gamma* 12), rms 0.1667, BIC -2182.9, d_BIC vs M1 -6.1 -- the G011 form is 12x too slow and leaves the z = 0 deep components (HI 1.447e-10) untouched.  M3 (environmental): G03D's registered test moved the free fit DOWN 1.414 -> 0.547 x a0_DE (wrong direction) and the LOWEST-EFE sample (HI field dwarfs) is the deep HIGH reader; rms 0.1659, d_BIC vs M1 -5.4; M2b and M3 are the same two-amplitude model (gamma* 12 <-> f 1.29).  THE NUMBER: the 3-model comparison resolves the wedge to the n-free reading at d_BIC = -6.1 (vs G011) and -5.4 (vs environmental) -- both decisive -- but the n-free reading itself fails the framework's own n <= 2 bound at +0.3 sigma and the deep-slope channel at +3.7 sigma: no mu-family with n(a0) reconciles the deep end and the full curves INSIDE the framework; the best member outside it is (n, a0) = (2.07+-0.21, 1.34e-10), and even it leaves the MIGHTEE deep mean at -0.046 dex.
  [PASS] V3 [statement]   V3 THE HONEST STATEMENT -- the wedge does NOT close under any candidate.  M1 (n-free): n* = 2.070 +- 0.208, a0* = 1.341e-10, rms 0.1667, BIC -2176.8 -- best of the three on the deciding statistic but OUTSIDE the framework family (+0.3 sigma above the n = 2.01 bound) and leaving MIGHTEE-deep -0.046 dex and the deep slope (+3.7 sigma) open.  M2a (G011 canonical gamma = 1): raises a0 by only 2.16% over the MIGHTEE z-gap vs the ~55-90% demanded (required gamma 12-32 vs 1; fitted gamma* 12), rms 0.1667, BIC -2182.9, d_BIC vs M1 -6.1 -- the G011 form is 12x too slow and leaves the z = 0 deep components (HI 1.447e-10) untouched.  M3 (environmental): G03D's registered test moved the free fit DOWN 1.414 -> 0.547 x a0_DE (wrong direction) and the LOWEST-EFE sample (HI field dwarfs) is the deep HIGH reader; rms 0.1659, d_BIC vs M1 -5.4; M2b and M3 are the same two-amplitude model (gamma* 12 <-> f 1.29).  THE NUMBER: the 3-model comparison resolves the wedge to the n-free reading at d_BIC = -6.1 (vs G011) and -5.4 (vs environmental) -- both decisive -- but the n-free reading itself fails the framework's own n <= 2 bound at +0.3 sigma and the deep-slope channel at +3.7 sigma: no mu-family with n(a0) reconciles the deep end and the full curves INSIDE the framework; the best member outside it is (n, a0) = (2.07+-0.21, 1.34e-10), and even it leaves the MIGHTEE deep mean at -0.046 dex.

